  "rationale": "ExprTyped.give uses take; .new requires a declaration and ArgsTyped at the entire declared classes; ArgsTyped.nil/cons threads environments left to right and fixes exact arity; .weaken uses Subtype. The extra Lean well-formedness/normalization premises express the chapter's global convention from environments, not operational-success hypotheses. The three displayed rules and first-pass restriction match these constructors, including rejection of partial arguments when a whole class is required.",
